    Batch suite-compliance lookups to fit the monitor's 60s budget
    
    Rebuild of ebec6ab onto current main (records-only delta). The checker ran
    `git show`/`git rev-parse` per commit and per candidate over 1141 first-parent
    changes: 71.1 s wall against the Judiciary monitor's 60 s budget, so the lens
    intermittently reported `unreadable` (measurement outage, not a red suite).
    
    Two behaviour-preserving batched lookups: one `git log --first-parent
    --diff-merges=first-parent -- records/suite-status.json` prefilter (keeping the
    first_parent_paths check), and one `git rev-list --format=%H %T` commit->tree
    map replacing a `git rev-parse <commit>^{tree}` subprocess per change and per
    candidate. Every reading now records `wall_seconds`.
    
    Measured on the canonical checkout with the same changes: 71.1 s -> 32.4 s
    wall; status/count/change fields identical to the unmodified checker (1133
    unreadable, 0 violations, 0 red-main, measured). No status semantics changed.

